WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.653
Fritz and Marie looked at the nutcracker in amazement.

2
00:00:12.654 --> 00:00:16.477
They listened eagerly as their godfather continued the tale.

3
00:00:16.478 --> 00:00:24.439
"Inside the princess' nursery were the king, queen, the nutcracker, and a small crowd of people.

4
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:30.082
And, of course, there was the Mouse Queen, who had just tripped the nutcracker.

5
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:36.453
The princess was beautiful again, but the once-handsome nutcracker was now ugly.

6
00:00:36.454 --> 00:00:39.265
The Mouse Queen lay on the nursery floor.

7
00:00:39.266 --> 00:00:44.930
As she slowly died, she muttered, 'I will have my revenge.

8
00:00:44.931 --> 00:00:49.394
Even though I may die, my son will never forget.'

9
00:00:49.395 --> 00:00:54.952
But everyone ignored her and rejoiced that the princess was beautiful again.

10
00:00:54.953 --> 00:00:56.936
Many years passed.

11
00:00:56.937 --> 00:01:02.762
The nutcracker lived in the palace and was a good and kind young man.

12
00:01:02.763 --> 00:01:06.419
Before long it was time for the princess to get married.

13
00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:11.983
The king reminded her that she must marry the nutcracker, but she refused.

14
00:01:11.984 --> 00:01:15.519
'He is too ugly,' she protested.

15
00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:22.918
The king and queen could not change the princess' mind, so they asked the nutcracker to leave the palace.

16
00:01:22.919 --> 00:01:25.445
Reluctantly he agreed and left."

17
00:01:25.446 --> 00:01:29.226
"Where is the nutcracker man now?" Marie asked.

18
00:01:29.227 --> 00:01:32.349
"He's right here," said Godfather.

19
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:37.034
The children gasped and inspected the nutcracker more closely.

20
00:01:37.035 --> 00:01:40.335
"I don't think he's ugly; he just looks different.

21
00:01:40.336 --> 00:01:43.350
There's nothing wrong with that," said Marie.

22
00:01:43.351 --> 00:01:46.478
"I think the princess worried too much about looks.

23
00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:50.643
She should remember that people can be beautiful on the inside."

24
00:01:50.644 --> 00:01:54.779
"You're a good girl, Marie," said her godfather.

25
00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.117
"What happened to the mice?" asked Fritz.

26
00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:01.451
"The Mouse Queen said her son would take his revenge."

27
00:02:01.452 --> 00:02:04.627
"Oh, he did," said their godfather.

28
00:02:04.628 --> 00:02:10.416
"But that's a story for another night. It's late and you must go to bed now.

29
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:16.020
Tomorrow's a big day. It's Christmas!"

30
00:02:16.021 --> 00:02:22.268
"I'm not tired," said Fritz, "and I can't sleep until I know the story's ending."

31
00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:25.939
"I'll tell you this," said their godfather in a whisper.

32
00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:32.789
"The Mouse King and the nutcracker fought in front of the Christmas tree, and the nutcracker won.

33
00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:35.971
Now go to bed, my dears."

34
00:02:35.972 --> 00:02:41.188
Marie was tired, but she was glad the nutcracker had defeated the Mouse King.

35
00:02:41.189 --> 00:02:45.970
She slept and dreamed of kings and queens and princesses and mice.

36
00:02:45.971 --> 00:02:52.233
In the middle of the night, Marie woke suddenly because she heard voices in the living room.

37
00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.597
Marie quickly got out of bed.

38
00:02:54.598 --> 00:02:59.233
The living room was dark except for the dim glow coming from the fireplace.

39
00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:02.770
But it was enough to see something moving near the Christmas tree.

40
00:03:02.771 --> 00:03:07.489
There was a strange shadow on the wall. Marie was scared.

41
00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:11.988
Then Marie saw him. It was the Mouse King, son of the Mouse Queen.

42
00:03:11.989 --> 00:03:17.637
His eyes glowed red, his face was like a rat's, and he wore a crown of rubies.

43
00:03:17.638 --> 00:03:25.610
The Mouse King looked across the room, and he called out, "I have to avenge my mother's death. Are you ready?"

44
00:03:25.611 --> 00:03:29.602
The nutcracker advanced without speaking. He seemed to be smiling.

45
00:03:29.603 --> 00:03:33.497
The Mouse King swiftly drew his sword and charged the nutcracker.

46
00:03:33.498 --> 00:03:40.704
Marie screamed, but the nutcracker also drew his sword and easily dodged the Mouse King's first attack.

47
00:03:40.705 --> 00:03:48.512
The Mouse King and the nutcracker battled back and forth across the living-room floor; their tiny swords clashed in the dim light.

48
00:03:48.513 --> 00:03:56.899
Marie had one hand over her mouth and one hand over her eyes, but she could see everything between her fingers.

49
00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.816
Both the nutcracker and the Mouse King fought hard and long.

50
00:04:00.817 --> 00:04:04.265
Marie knew someone would make a deadly mistake soon.

51
00:04:04.266 --> 00:04:08.458
She saw the nutcracker fall and gasped. She had to act.

52
00:04:08.459 --> 00:04:12.525
Marie pulled off her shoe and hurled it straight at the Mouse King.

53
00:04:12.526 --> 00:04:16.054
Her shoe hit him in the head.

54
00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:21.666
Poof! Like magic the Mouse King was gone, but the nutcracker was gone too!

55
00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:25.847
"The battle is over," said a handsome prince standing next to her.

56
00:04:25.848 --> 00:04:29.950
"Yes," said Marie, "but where is the nutcracker?"

57
00:04:29.951 --> 00:04:35.779
"I am here," said the handsome man. "I am the nutcracker."

58
00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:41.441
"But my nutcracker was ugly! You are so handsome," exclaimed Marie.

59
00:04:41.442 --> 00:04:45.370
"The Mouse Queen's spell is finally broken," said the nutcracker.

60
00:04:45.371 --> 00:04:49.819
The nutcracker prince looked at Marie with his kind eyes and gentle smile.

61
00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:56.001
Marie's eyes twinkled as she said, "Merry Christmas, nutcracker!"

62
00:04:56.002 --> 00:05:00.250
"Marie, get up!" called Fritz. He came into the living room.

63
00:05:00.251 --> 00:05:02.348
"Why are you sleeping here?"

64
00:05:02.349 --> 00:05:07.184
Marie slowly sat up. "Where's the handsome prince?" she asked.

65
00:05:07.185 --> 00:05:11.022
Then she realized it was all a dream. She smiled.

66
00:05:11.023 --> 00:05:17.235
Godfather had given her two gifts this Christmas: a nutcracker and his story.
